## Context

Tracker 0406 restructures the build into one .mk per phase. Its S1
(author-ratified 2026-06-04): retire `slides/inputs/generated/` so P3
has a single deliverable tree, `report/inputs/generated/`. Done before
the render.mk extraction (S2) so render.mk is written once against the
final layout.

The slides tree is already almost empty: slides consume nearly all
artifacts via `../report/inputs/generated/`. Only 2 tracked files
remain, BOTH with name collisions against different-content report
files, so the move is a move-with-rename:

| slides/inputs/generated/ | producer | destination |
|--------------------------|----------|-------------|
| `macros.tex` | `tabulate_macros --census-csv census_bars.csv` (rule at analysis.mk:377-380; report's `macros.tex` is tabulate_macros WITHOUT the flag — different content) | `report/inputs/generated/macros_slides.tex` |
| `tab_exp2_2x2.tex` | FR variant (`ANALYSIS_EXP2_2X2_FR_TEX`, analysis.mk:53; report's is EN) | `report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_2x2_fr.tex` |

NOT a dedup: `macros_census.tex` (plot_method_convergence) is a third,
unrelated generator — leave it alone. No content changes: `git mv` +
repoint, never regenerate (mart staleness hazard, 0383).

## Relevant files

- `experiments/analysis.mk` — `ANALYSIS_SLIDE_GEN` (l.38),
  `ANALYSIS_EXP2_2X2_FR_TEX` (l.53), `ANALYSIS_SLIDE_MACROS` (l.56),
  slide-macros rule (l.375-380), `exp2-analysis-report` aggregate
- root `Makefile` — `SLIDE_GEN` var (l.10) + its uses
- `slides/Makefile` — `ROOT_SLIDE_GEN` (l.8) + prerequisite lists
- `slides/slides.tex`, `slides/slides-en.tex` — l.16
  `\InputIfFileExists{inputs/generated/macros}` →
  `{../report/inputs/generated/macros_slides}`; l.353
  `\input{inputs/generated/tab_exp2_2x2.tex}` →
  `{../report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_2x2_fr.tex}`
- `.gitignore` — drop the `slides/inputs/generated/*` block + its
  negations (added by 0405/PR #690)
- `tests/` — `test_slides_build_clean_room`, `test_make_slides_prereqs`,
  the 0405 adherence test; grep tests/ for `slides/inputs/generated`
- `docs/pipeline-phases.md` — manifest rows for the two moved files;
  P3 section now states the single-tree rule
- Sweep: `grep -rn "slides/inputs/generated" --exclude-dir=.git .` must
  end empty (translation script 0389, scripts/, src/, CI workflows)

## Actions

1. Red test first: adherence test asserting no reference to
   `slides/inputs/generated` in Makefiles, .tex, tests, scripts, src,
   and that the directory does not exist in the git index.
2. `git mv` the two files to their renamed destinations.
3. Repoint producers (analysis.mk vars/rules), consumers (slides .tex
   ×2), and orchestration (root Makefile, slides/Makefile prereqs).
4. Reconcile .gitignore (delete the slides-tree block; ensure the two
   renamed files are covered by the existing
   `!report/inputs/generated/...` negation scheme — they are .tex, which
   is not wildcard-ignored, so just confirm).
5. Update tests + docs/pipeline-phases.md manifest.
6. Delete untracked leftovers in `slides/inputs/generated/` (regenerable
   intermediates untracked by 0405) and the empty directory.

## Test

The adherence test of action 1 (red today: analysis.mk, Makefile,
slides/Makefile, slides.tex, slides-en.tex, .gitignore all reference the
tree). Green after actions 2-6.

## Verification

- [ ] `grep -rn "slides/inputs/generated" --exclude-dir=.git .` empty
- [ ] `slides/inputs/generated/` absent from index and working tree
- [ ] `test_slides_build_clean_room` + `test_make_slides_prereqs` green
- [ ] 0405 adherence test (no tracked-but-ignored) still green
- [ ] `make slides` builds (tectonic, artifacts only) — both FR and EN
- [ ] `make check` green

## Invariants

- No artifact content changes — `git mv` only, never regenerate (0383)
- Report tree files untouched except the two arrivals
- CI (docs-build.yml) green; clean-room tests keep passing

## Exit criteria

- `slides/inputs/generated/` gone — tree, references, ignore lines
- The two artifacts live renamed in `report/inputs/generated/`, slides
  build consumes them from there
- Guard test prevents reintroduction
